WEBVTT

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.040
Takkun, you curious?

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.590
Yeah.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.220
I'm curious to know why 
you're dressed that way.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.780
You can take a small peek if you want.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:16.950
Here.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.530
It's all scales underneath.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.680
The situation is what's important here!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.520
What situation?

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.830
Come on, just look!

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.090
They really have no future together...

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.640
But it's just scales!

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:27.240
Yeah...

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.640
Just look!

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.950
I don't want to look at scales!

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.090
<b>Muromi-san on the Shore</b>

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.090
<b>Episode 7
"The Boy, Kappa, and Muromi-san"</b>

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.100
I haven't gone river fishing in a while.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.720
It's nice to relax and

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.270
let your lure just float there 
every now and then.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.420
Oh, there's one.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.960
Oh, no!

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.640
<b>Got a bad feeling...</b>

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:18.820
<i>Got a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:23.530
Takkun, you perv!

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:24.710
Give that back?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.120
I knew it'd be you!

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.080
What are you even doing?

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.110
I'm just coming back from 
meeting a friend I know

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.450
who lives upstream.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.140
You know you have to watch out 
for UV rays this time of year.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.210
It's a hat?

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.300
It look good?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.910
And that beak?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:41.890
It's a mask.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.160
And that shell?

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.980
I need it to carry stuff in.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.210
I mean, I couldn't go there 
empty-handed, ya know?

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.360
It's a bag?!

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.980
Care for a snack?

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.270
I got a bunch of Japanese yams in return.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.570
In return...

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.820
In return...

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.030
<i>I've just seen the kappa's true identity!</i>

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.650
<i>Just maybe all of Japan's legends, 
weird creatures, and monsters</i>

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.160
<i>have been the same person all along!</i>

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.490
<i>And it wasn't a person.</i>

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:08.500
<i>It was this mermaid!</i>

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.370
Hey...

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.940
Takkun.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.730
You're river fishing today?

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.910
What's so good about fish that 
can only live in fresh water?

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.720
You know I can live in both 
fresh and salt water?

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.500
Hurry home and rest.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.980
And keep warm.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.490
You're right.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.520
Then Takkun...

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.230
What are you doing?!

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.200
You warm me up!

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.650
Hey! Get away!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:35.820
You're cold and all wet!

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.580
And you're all scaly!

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:38.580
Muromi.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.030
It's a ka-ka-ka...

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.610
Save me!

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.820
<i>He's going to remove 
the ball from my butt!</i>

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:49.040
Kawabata-kun, what are you 
doing all the way downriver?

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.500
Kawabata-kun?

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.280
<b>Kawabata-kun</b>

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.260
Kappa?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.280
<b>Kappa</b>

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.430
You know him?

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.280
<b>You know him?</b>

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.760
I've got some pills for you.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.510
Take them and you should be 
feeling better overnight.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.590
You came all this way just 
to bring those to me?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.580
Thanks for that.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:02.560
I really appreciate the trouble.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.980
And what are you looking at?

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.090
I'll kick your ass.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.510
I knew this would happen!

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:10.720
<i>He's going to remove 
the ball from my butt!</i>

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:14.380
Now, now. You're done 
bringing me the medicine.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.380
Thanks. I'll return the favor sometime.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.400
On your way, now.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:20.610
Here.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.070
Shuwatch!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.840
Don't mind him.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.570
He doesn't like humans much.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.410
Much?! I thought he was gonna kill me!

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.550
Well, a long time ago,

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.130
Kawabata-kun's older brother 
was attacked by humans.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.300
Attacked by humans?

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.910
Kill it!

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.680
So that's what happened.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.880
Yeah, so he's been hard 
on humans since then.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.760
I can see why he'd pick fights with humans.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:02.260
So, what happened to his brother?

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.070
Oh, he's in Osaka now.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.180
So he's fine!

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.630
Nah, heard of the Zuiryuji temple?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:09.660
Z-Zuiryuji?! Y-You mean...

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:10.870
Yup!

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.790
That kappa mummy is 
Kawabata-kun's brother?!

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.160
<b>Brother</b>

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:18.320
They seem to be taking 
pretty good care of it,

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.880
so Kawabata-kun's not 
really sure what to do.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.450
Well, they are treating it 
like a religious artifact.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:26.280
By the way, it's not currently on display.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:32.070
Hey, Muromi-san, do you have a 
lot of strange friends like that?

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.770
Hm? Yeah, I do.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.100
The tsuchinoko being one.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.690
Tsuchinoko?!

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.150
Bitter!

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.150
Muromi-san!

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.610
<b>Somewhere in Kyushu</b>

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.880
Just so you know, I didn't 
come to this river to spawn!

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:53.910
Hey!

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.370
I'm here!

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.300
Hey, Muromi-san!

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.210
It's been a while.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:02.210
<b>Houman-san</b>

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:02.560
There we go.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.790
It's been a while, Houman-san.

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.990
Thanks for calling me out 
here again this year.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:11.280
Not at all. We couldn't start without you.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.930
I can't handle it all by myself 
during this time of year.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:16.930
I mean, just look at all of 
these poisonous mushrooms!

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:21.460
Wow, look at that!

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.400
It's pretty bad this year.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.670
Kawabata-kun's here too.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:29.110
Oh, Kawabata-kun! Hey there!

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.480
Oh, it's you, Muromi.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:33.580
You here to pick mushrooms too?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.040
Thanks for those yams the other day.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.100
No problem.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.820
That kid you picked a fight 
with is still scared.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.000
The poor boy.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.580
Oh, yams?

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.110
That sounds good.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.640
It'd be nice if these were 
matsutake mushrooms,

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.220
but they're all poisonous.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.830
Muromi, how's the sea?

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:53.030
Anything going on down there?

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.930
Going on?

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.910
The sea's always changing.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.540
The water level changes 
due to the moon's pull,

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.140
the currents change with the 
concentration of salt,

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.850
animals born in the sea are going up to land,

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.330
and there's the water cycle,

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.600
the cycle, cycle...

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.450
Cycle, cycle, cycle...

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.830
Stop it!

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.290
I'm stupid for even asking.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.750
All right!

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.770
If you don't have any more questions,

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:24.740
we're going to pull all 
these up until the sun sets!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.210
<b>Scream!</b>

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.220
There we go!

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.250
<b>Scream!</b>

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.290
<b>Ahh!</b>

00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:34.500
There!

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.390
All of you, shut up!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.390
Ah!

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:39.350
Oh, no!

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:40.970
Don't!

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.540
<b>Don't...</b>

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.040
Did we have these last year?

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.430
No, these are obviously foreign.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:47.940
Foreign?

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.160
They've got vegetation 
like this in the West,

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.800
but I didn't know they had 
ones shaped like mushrooms.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.040
So what are we going to 
do with all of these?

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.670
Well, eat them, of course!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.170
<b>Hahaha!</b>

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:06.900
Poison. Totally poison!

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.930
How about this one?

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:12.740
Ecstasy!

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.590
The world's spinning.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.850
The whole earth's spinning.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:20.990
This is great!

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:22.830
My tongue's going numb. 
These are excellent.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.480
Poison isn't poisonous to 
us unknown creatures,

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.970
Poison isn't poisonous to 
us unknown creatures,

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.320
but make sure you don't 
try this at home!

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:30.170
but make sure you don't 
try this at home!

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.860
Hii-chan here!

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.320
Muromi-san...

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:38.270
<b>A few days later</b>

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:44.960
He's here!

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.300
Wait a second.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.200
Is Muromi here yet?

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.990
I'm not really here waiting for Muromi-san,

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:58.930
so I don't know if she'll be here today!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.800
So you don't know, huh?

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.120
<i>This sucks. I don't know 
how to handle this guy.</i>

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.360
<i>He's not even human, and he's scary.</i>

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:13.280
Here.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.100
What is it?

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:15.880
Eat up.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:17.450
Cucumber.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:20.910
Cucumber...

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.280
You don't want it?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.640
I'm goo—

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:26.620
I'll take it!

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:29.370
<i>So Kappa really do eat 
cucumbers then.</i>

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.550
<i>This isn't ripe!</i>

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:37.710
Oh, i-it's just a little stronger than 
the ones I'm used to eating!

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.360
Huh? You can tell?

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:40.140
What?

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.470
That's because...

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.060
All the ones you're used
 to seeing at the market

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.690
are grown in soil with reduced fertility.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.540
This cucumber was grown in 
fertile soil in the same conditions

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.270
that wild ones would grow in, 
unlike the farmed kind.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:52.600
They taste a little different 
than normal cucumbers.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.650
<i>Oh, man. He's really into this.</i>

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.650
It's because they try to mass 
produce them, you know?

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.530
That's how it is.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:05.280
<b>Silence.</b>

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:06.540
Umm...

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:13.790
<b>Silence.</b>

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:16.550
How long have you known Muromi-san?

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.550
A long time.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:18.680
<b>Conversation over.</b>

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.640
<b>It's like we can't have a real conversation.</b>

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.760
<i>It's like we can't have 
a real conversation.</i>

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:24.800
Muromi-san's still not here...

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.230
Do you know if she is going 
to come today, Kawabata-san?

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.190
I've told her.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:31.400
I texted her.

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:33.820
You have one?!

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:34.750
Got a problem with that?

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:37.030
Not at all. They're useful, aren't they?

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:39.740
<b>Silence.</b>

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.780
<i>Hey, Muromi-san. Save me already.</i>

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.410
<i>Where are you, anyway?</i>

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.240
Huh?

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.620
Just come out if you're here!

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.710
Don't cry, don't cry.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.550
I was just wondering what guys talk about.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.630
There, there.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.780
I'm not crying.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:00.700
Muromi!

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.780
It's not good to eavesdrop.

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:03.720
Here.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.960
It's some of my harvest.

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:07.290
Shuwatch!

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:09.730
Thanks, Kawabata-kun!

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.230
He sure left really fast!

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.700
Well, he's a pretty simple-spoken guy.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.100
Look at this.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.890
Thick, bumpy, and full of goodness.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:24.330
Looks tasty!

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:26.040
This isn't ripe.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.590
You know that Kawabata-kun 
doesn't like humans,

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:31.800
but he likes you, Takkun.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:35.580
I mean, he gave you one of his crop.

00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:38.840
For a kappa, you'd have to be 
pretty close for that to happen.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.580
<b>Confused.</b>

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:42.030
I don't understand him at all.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.470
I guess he's a good guy, after all.

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:53.100
Kawabata-kun, thank you for 
those fresh cucumbers.

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:56.270
I ate a ton of them whole, 
so I got round like a tsuchinoko.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.900
That was your cue for a retort.

00:11:58.290 --> 00:11:59.150
You sure are laid back.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.440
Who was America's thirteenth president?

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:06.220
Next Time
"Muromi-san and the Nice(?) Type"

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.480
Millard Fillmore.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:03.420
Impressive!
